Sub-problem-Id: 4; Sub-problem: What is the absolute difference between \(\pi\) and \(\frac{22}{7}\)?;

Answer: The value of \(\frac{22}{7}\) as a decimal is \(3.142857\ldots\). Therefore, the absolute difference between \(\pi\) and \(\frac{22}{7}\) is \(|\pi-\frac{22}{7}|=|3.1415926...-3.142857...|=0.0006494...\).

